'''Coco's Village Wash Spring''' (or simply Wash Spring) is a [[Contraption]] located near [[Coco's Village]].

== Description ==
[[File:Wash Spring Seal Redraw.png|left|thumb|120px|<small>A Redraw of the Casting Seal as seen in [[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]].</small>]] 
The [[Spells|Casting Seal]] contains a [[Sigils#Repetition|Sigil of Repetition]] connected to two [[Sigils#Purification|Sigils of Purification]]. Two [[Signs#Columns|Signs of Columns]] facing outwards are placed on either side of the Purification Sigil, making for a total of four. Two [[Signs#Partition|Signs of Partition]] point inwards, towards the Repetition Sigil, separating three [[Signs#Refuse|Signs of Refuse]] each, adding up to six of them total.{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 146}}

Upon activation, this spell will cause the spring to shine brightly and purify its waters of any waste or contaminants found inside, making for a clean and reliable source of water.{{Ref|a|1}}{{Ref|m|1|7-10}} It is unclear just how long this spell lasts, especially given there are no [[Witches|witches]] currently living in [[Coco]]'s village to maintain it.{{Ref|a|1}}{{Ref|m|1|19}}

The spring is located in [[Naakiwan Downs]], specifically a forest nearby Coco's village. It is a small, shallow pool of water connected to two streams, with a small stone bridge placed above one of them. It is surrounded by lush vegetation and paved with small stepping stones.{{Ref|a|1}}{{Ref|m|1|7-10}} Carved onto these stepping stones are Casting Seals that activate upon being stepped on.{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 146}} Nearby wildlife include a female [[Trihorn Deer]] and a [[Blushing Bride|Blushing Bride Butterfly]].{{Cite}} In the manga, some clothes are seen set out to dry nearby the spring.{{Ref|m|1|10}}

