== History & Usage ==
At an unknown point prior to the events of the story, a witch carves casting seals into the stones of a local spring near Coco's village.

In [[Chapter 1]], Coco is seen using the Wash Spring to hand-wash her laundry. She pours soap into its waters and is observed by a trihorn deer. Once she is finished, she notices the deer and assures it that the water will go back to normal. Upon stepping out of the spring, the water does just that.{{Ref|a|1}}{{Ref|m|1|7-10}}

In [[Chapter 61]], Coco presents her [[Portable Waste Purification Pot|Purification Pot]] for the [[Silver Eve Procession]]. Her motivation behind creating the spell and contraption is to provide easier access to clean water, recalling how she'd need to take multiple trips to the spring to dump out their dirty water and retrieve fresh, clean water.{{Ref|m|61|16}}

